invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: check_required stops requiring signature_algorithms of a hello that
  offers no PSK, so the server would go on to sign a CertificateVerify
  with a scheme the client never said it could verify. RFC 9846 §9.2
  makes the extension mandatory there and names missing_extension
  (rfc9846.txt:4595-4605). test/srv_parser_tests.h drops it from the
  golden hello and requires that alert.

--- old
    uint16_t auth = SRV_EXT_SIGNATURE_ALGORITHMS | SRV_EXT_SUPPORTED_GROUPS;
--- new
    uint16_t auth = SRV_EXT_SUPPORTED_GROUPS;
